<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  {% if state.meta.demo %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">{% endif %}
  <meta name="description" content="Theoxenia Mission Control — an evidence-first radio data search status page.">
  <title>Theoxenia — Mission control</title>
  <meta property="og:title" content="Theoxenia — Mission control">
  <meta property="og:description" content="An open lab for radio signals in public telescope data. Explore what we measured, how we tested it, and what the evidence can actually tell us.">
  {% if og_image %}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ og_image }}">
  {% endif %}
  <link rel="alternate" type="application/feed+json" title="Theoxenia survivors" href="feed.json">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a class="wordmark" href="index.html"><span aria-hidden="true">⊹</span> Theoxenia</a>
      <div>{% if stories %}<a href="investigations.html">Investigations</a><a href="research.html">Research &amp; contributions</a>{% else %}<a href="#hero-heading">The evidence</a><a href="#method-heading">The method</a>{% endif %}<a href="evidence.html">Lab notebook</a><a href="{{ repo_url }}">GitHub ↗</a></div>
    </nav>
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="header-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">An open observatory · Mission control</p>
        <h1>Welcome the unknown.<br><span class="title-muted">Follow the evidence.</span></h1>
        <p class="subtitle">An open lab for radio signals in public telescope data. Explore what we measured, how we tested it, and what the evidence can actually tell us.</p>
        {% if stories %}<div class="action-row"><a class="button-link button-primary" href="investigations.html">Follow an investigation ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="#totals-heading">See the recorded work ↓</a></div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="status-pill status-pill--{{ status.tone }}" aria-label="Worker status: {{ status.label }}">
        <span class="status-dot{% if status.is_live %} status-dot--live{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>{{ status.label }}</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      {% if stories %}
      <section class="section-block home-investigations" aria-labelledby="investigations-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The field guide · Volume 01</p><h2 id="investigations-heading">Three questions. An open notebook.</h2></div><p>Follow a known signal, inspect a real archive search, and explore the limits of our detector. Every story opens its evidence.</p></div>{% include "investigation-cards.html.j2" %}</section>
      {% endif %}
      {% if synthetic_only %}
      <div class="demo-banner" role="note"><strong>Synthetic calibration session.</strong><span>These are generated test signals, not telescope observations.</span></div>
      {% elif state.meta.demo %}
      <div class="demo-banner" role="note">
        <strong>Demo data — every number here is a placeholder.</strong>
        <span>M0 only: no live worker or telescope observations are included.</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if not state.meta.demo %}
      <p class="snapshot-note">Recorded evidence · Observational totals exclude synthetic practice runs. This page is a snapshot; reload to see a newer build.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <section class="ticker-panel" aria-label="Search ticker">
        <p>{{ ticker }}</p>
        <span>State built {{ generated_at_text }}</span>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="totals-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="totals-heading">What has been searched</h2>
          <p>Every count opens its supporting run manifests.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-grid">
          {% for metric in metrics %}
          <a class="metric-card{% if metric.key == 'unexplained' %} metric-card--review{% endif %}" href="{{ metric.href }}">
            <span class="metric-label">{{ metric.label }}</span>
            <span class="metric-value">{{ metric.value }}</span>
            {% if metric.unit %}<span class="metric-unit">{{ metric.unit }}</span>{% endif %}
          </a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="hero-heading">Proof the detector works: Voyager 1</h2>
          <p>Start with something we know. A recorded Voyager carrier tests whether the pipeline can recover a human transmitter. A positive control establishes a starting point, not a universal sensitivity limit.</p>
        </div>
        {% if state.hero %}
        <article class="hero-card">
          <a class="hero-image-link" href="{{ hero_manifest_url }}" aria-label="Open the Voyager run manifest">
            <img src="{{ state.hero.image_url }}" alt="Voyager 1 waterfall from the run manifest: a narrow carrier across frequency and time" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ state.hero.experiment }} · Known transmitter</p>
            <h3>A faint line. A known origin.</h3>
            <p>The waterfall shows received power across frequency and time. Follow the narrow carrier, then inspect the exact measurement.</p>
            <p>Frequency <strong>{{ "%.6f"|format(state.hero.freq_mhz) }} MHz</strong></p>
            <p>Drift <strong>{{ "%+.3f"|format(state.hero.drift_hz_s) }} Hz/s</strong></p>
            <p>SNR <strong>{{ "%.1f"|format(state.hero.snr) }}</strong></p>
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ hero_manifest_url }}">Open the run manifest</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        {% else %}
        <div class="empty-panel">
          <h3>Waiting for EXP-001</h3>
          {% if state.meta.demo %}
          <p>No Voyager result is available in this M0 demo.</p>
          {% else %}
          <p>No Voyager result is available yet.</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </section>

      <section class="section-block method-section" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The method</p><h2 id="method-heading">Look at the star. Look away. Repeat.</h2></div><p>A signal in an OFF scan fails the direction test. A signal confined to ON scans still needs further checks.</p></div>
        <div class="cadence-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Illustration, not measured data: six scans alternate target A with off-target positions B, C, and D. ON-only presence is a reason to check further, not a conclusion.">
          {% for role in ['A', 'B', 'A', 'C', 'A', 'D'] %}
          <div class="scan{% if role == 'A' %} scan--on{% endif %}"><span>{{ 'On target' if role == 'A' else 'Off target' }}</span><strong>{{ role }}</strong><div class="scan-trace" aria-hidden="true"></div><small>{{ 'Look at the star' if role == 'A' else 'Compare the sky' }}</small></div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="figure-note">Method illustration · not a measured waterfall. Surviving this comparison does not establish a source or origin.</p>
        <div class="method-steps"><p><strong>Observe</strong> Read a bounded frequency window from public recordings.</p><p><strong>Compare</strong> Check drift, repeatability, OFF scans and known transmitters.</p><p><strong>Reproduce</strong> Keep the inputs, parameters and result together in a run record.</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="map-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="map-heading">Where we have looked</h2>
          <p>Each point opens a recorded cadence. The map shows where we looked, not how much of the sky we have ruled out. Synthetic coordinates are excluded from the observational view.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="plot-card sky-card">
          {{ sky_markup | safe }}
          <ul class="map-legend" aria-label="Sky map legend">
            <li><span class="legend-dot legend-dot--searched" aria-hidden="true"></span>Searched</li>
            <li><span class="legend-dot legend-dot--running" aria-hidden="true"></span>In progress</li>
            <li><span class="legend-dot legend-dot--survivor" aria-hidden="true"></span>Survivor</li>
            <li><span class="legend-dot legend-dot--failed" aria-hidden="true"></span>Failed pair</li>
          </ul>
          <ul class="visually-hidden" aria-label="Manifest links for searched pointings">
            {% for pointing in map_accessible_pointings %}
            <li><a href="cadences/{{ pointing.cadence_id }}/index.html">{{ pointing.target }} cadence page</a> · <a href="{{ pointing.manifest_url }}">{{ pointing.target }} — {{ pointing.status.value }}, {{ pointing.hits }} hits</a></li>
            {% else %}
            <li>No pointings have been recorded.</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="floor-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="floor-heading">How faint a signal we would catch</h2>
          <p>A detector must earn its null results. We inject signals with known strengths and drifts, then measure how often they return. The grid shows a recorded calibration run.</p>
          <p>Synthetic setigen injections only — not telescope observations. Recovery is computed from the recorded grid.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="floor-layout">
          <div class="plot-card floor-card">
            {{ floor_markup | safe }}
          </div>
          <div class="floor-copy">
            {% if state.detection_floor %}
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ state.detection_floor.experiment }} · {{ state.detection_floor.run_id }}</p>
            <p>{{ state.detection_floor.summary }}</p>
            <p>Each cell records the fraction of injected signals recovered; no cell is observational evidence.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ floor_manifest_url }}">Open the injection run manifest</a>
            {% if floor_ci_url %}
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ floor_ci_url }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the CI run</a>
            {% endif %}
            {% else %}
            <h3>Waiting for EXP-002</h3>
            {% if state.meta.demo %}
            <p>No recovery grid is available in this M0 demo.</p>
            {% else %}
            <p>No recovery grid is available yet.</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="verdict-heading">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Follow the result</p><h2 id="verdict-heading">What happened to the hits?</h2></div><p>All recorded verdicts, including hits outside the preview gallery. Each bar links to the supporting run records.</p></div>
        <div class="verdict-chart">
          {% for row in verdict_rows %}
          <a class="verdict-row" href="runs/index.html#hits"><span>{{ row.label }}</span><span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill bar-fill--{{ row.key }}" style="width: {{ row.percent }}%"></span></span><strong>{{ row.count }}</strong></a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="figure-note">One first-fitting verdict per hit. A zero means none in these records; it is not a limit on signals elsewhere.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="gallery-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="gallery-heading">Latest hits, and the checks applied.</h2>
          <p>Selected measured hits, newest first. Each classification describes the recorded checks; it does not identify a physical source. A survivor needs further investigation.</p>
        </div>
        {% if gallery %}
        <div class="gallery-grid">
          {% for item in gallery %}
          <article class="hit-card">
            <a class="hit-thumbnail" href="hits/{{ item.hit_id }}.html" aria-label="Open the hit page for {{ item.target }}">
              <img src="{{ item.thumbnail_url }}" alt="Recorded hit summary for {{ item.target }} at {{ "%.6f"|format(item.freq_mhz) }} MHz" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </a>
            <div class="hit-copy">
              <p class="verdict-badge verdict-badge--{{ item.verdict.value|lower }}">{{ item.badge_text }}</p>
              <h3>{{ item.target }}</h3>
              <p class="hit-metrics">{{ "%.6f"|format(item.freq_mhz) }} MHz · {{ "%+.3f"|format(item.drift_hz_s) }} Hz/s · SNR {{ "%.1f"|format(item.snr) }}</p>
              <p>{{ item.explanation }}</p>
              <a class="text-link" href="hits/{{ item.hit_id }}.html">Open the hit page</a>
              <a class="text-link" href="{{ item.manifest_url }}">Open run manifest</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% else %}
        <div class="empty-panel">
          <h3>No hits yet</h3>
          {% if state.meta.demo %}
          <p>There are no run manifests with hits in this demo state.</p>
          {% else %}
          <p>There are no cadence manifests with hit records yet.</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </section>

      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="later-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="later-heading">Beyond the radio search</h2>
          <p>Two early research tracks use the same rule: a source, a method, and a record of what remains uncertain.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="later-grid">
          {% if later_bluebook %}
          <article class="empty-panel">
            <p class="eyebrow">Archive lab · Early work</p><h3>Reading the historical record</h3>
            <p>Project Blue Book document extraction. These runs measure extraction work; an incident map and corpus-level validation are still pending.</p><p>{{ later_bluebook.summary }}</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ later_bluebook.manifest_url }}">Open the run manifest</a>
          </article>
          {% else %}
          <article class="empty-panel">
            <h3>Disclosure, Project Blue Book incident map: not started</h3>
          </article>
          {% endif %}
          {% if later_nearearth %}
          <article class="empty-panel">
            <p class="eyebrow">Context lab · Early work</p><h3>Put an event in context</h3>
            <p>Public fireball and geomagnetic records for a historical window. Coverage gaps remain; absence in a catalogue does not explain an event.</p><p>{{ later_nearearth.summary }}</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ later_nearearth.manifest_url }}">Open the run manifest</a>
          </article>
          {% else %}
          <article class="empty-panel">
            <h3>Near-Earth baselines, CNEOS and Kp: not started</h3>
          </article>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-block contribute-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">An invitation to investigate</p><h2>Bring curiosity. Leave a reproducible trail.</h2><p>Inspect a run, challenge a check, or help improve a source reader. Null results and documented failures belong here too.</p></div><a class="button-link" href="{{ repo_url }}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Explore the contributor guide ↗</a></section>

      <section class="section-block read-this" aria-labelledby="reading-heading">
        <h2 id="reading-heading">How to read this page</h2>
        <p>Counts are computed from run manifests. A “survivor” has passed the checks recorded so far; it is not a conclusion. “Unexplained” is reserved for a reviewed record with the required sign-offs. {% if state.meta.demo %}The M0 badge remains visible so demo values cannot be mistaken for observations.{% else %}Every displayed result links to its supporting run manifest.{% endif %}</p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <p class="footer-motto">Prosaic first. Provenance always.</p><p>Code Apache-2.0 · Project-authored documentation CC BY 4.0 · Source data retains its original terms.</p>
      <p>{{ state.meta.data_credit }}</p>
      <p><a href="evidence.html">Lab notebook</a> · <a href="feed.json">Survivors feed</a> · <a href="sitemap.xml">Page list</a></p>
      <p><a href="{{ repo_url }}">Source code on GitHub</a></p>
      {% if mirror_url %}
      <p><a href="{{ mirror_url }}">GitHub Pages mirror</a> · static snapshot, not a live heartbeat</p>
      {% else %}
      <p>GitHub Pages mirror not yet deployed.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <p>State built {{ generated_at_text }} · Git {{ state.git_sha }} · Theoxenia {{ state.package_version }}</p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
